.TH PSTanhActivation 3 2024-01-03 "PsyC 0.9.4" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSTanhActivation\fR \- Tanh (hyperbolic tangent) activation function

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/activation.h>

.I
void  
.br
\fBPSTanhActivation\fR(\fIPSFloat *vec\fR, \fIPSFloat *dest\fR, \fIuint64_t len\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tanh (hyperbolic tangent) activation function for vectors. Hyperbolic tangent is computed on vector \fIvec\fR of length \fIlen\fR and stored into vector \fIdest\fR.
.br
If \fIdest\fR is \fINULL\fR, results will be stored into \fIvec\fR itself.
.br
The \fIopts\fR argument can be used to change default acceleration used to compute results (see \fIPSMathOpts\fR).
.br
The derivative of this function is \fIPSTanhDerivative\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1), PSTanhDerivative(3)
